1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,000
OK, everybody.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,100
I want to welcome Harry and his daughter Michelle

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,360
to Thanksgiving with us.

4
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:11,520
Thank you, Dr. Stewart.

5
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,800
Call me Philip.

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,600
OK.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
But first, I think we should take a moment

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,300
and remember the meaning of Thanksgiving.

9
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,600
Philip, I took Michelle to a school play

10
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,500
about the first Thanksgiving.

11
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,800
Well, why don't you tell us about that, Michelle?

12
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,300
Thanksgiving was about the Pilgrims,

13
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,300
the first settlers in America.

14
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,060
They shared the first harvest with the Indians

15
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:33,400
and gave thanks.

16
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,300
All right.

17
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,450
Then in that spirit let each of us give thanks.

18
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,200
Each in his own way.

19
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,750
Who wants to begin?

20
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:43,400
I will.

21
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:47,700
I give thanks for being here with my family and for being well,

22
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:49,190
so I can enjoy you all.

23
00:00:49,190 --> 00:00:50,610
All rihgt!

24
00:00:50,610 --> 00:00:53,100
We love you, Grandpa.

25
00:00:53,100 --> 00:01:00,100
I'd like to give thanks for a healthy year, a good job,

26
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:03,400
and for meeting Harry and Michelle.

27
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:05,600
We'd like to give thanks for meeting Susan

28
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:06,400
and the Stewart family.

29
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,500
I love you, Daddy.

30
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,800
Thanks, Harry.

31
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,200
That was very kind of you.

32
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:14,800
I'd like to give thanks for Grandpa coming to live with us.

33
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,900
And I'd also like to thank my math teacher

34
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:20,170
for giving me a passing grade.

35
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:23,880
And call me, Alexandra.

36
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:24,700
Oh, Robbie!

37
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:26,500
She'll call.

38
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,500
You go first, Marilyn.

39
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:29,500
I'm thinking.

40
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,000
You go first.

41
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,400
Well, you all know I'm working on my photo album.

42
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:39,300
It's not finished yet.

43
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:43,400
And I'd like to thank Marilyn for being so patient.

44
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,800
Thanks, Richard.

45
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,900
I should thank you for encouraging me

46
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:48,700
to keep working on my fashion designs.

47
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:53,600
I'm lucky to have a husband with an artistic eye.

48
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:58,500
Oh, we have a lot to be thankful for.

49
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,490
For the food on this table.

50
00:02:00,490 --> 00:02:02,100
Just like the Pilgrims.

51
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:04,300
I'll go along with that, Ellen.

52
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:09,900
Well, help me serve, Robbie.

53
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:11,400
It was a wonderful meal, Mrs. Stewart.

54
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,700
Thank you.

55
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:14,500
And now to see the end of the football game.

56
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:16,100
Exactly.

57
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:17,800
Where are you going, Philip?

58
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,700
Remember, the Michigan football game?

59
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:23,000
And Michigan needs a touchdown.

60
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,100
Did you forget something?

61
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,800
Dad, your famous apple pie.

62
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:29,100
Just let me see the score, Ellen.

63
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,300
Go ahead, Philip.

64
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:43,100
We should all take a little break before dessert.

65
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:47,100
Oh, who could that be?

66
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,100
Oh, it must be Alexandra.

67
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:51,300
I invited her to come by for dessert.

68
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:52,600
You did?

69
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:53,900
I like Ellen.

70
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,300
You know everyone, Alexandra.

71
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,800
No, she doesn't know Harry Bennett and his daughter Michelle.

72
00:02:58,800 --> 00:02:59,900
Nice to meet you.

73
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,200
Hi.

74
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,800
Hello, Alexandra.

75
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,100
Hi, Marilyn.

76
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:04,300
Hi, Susan.

77
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,400
Happy Thanksgiving.

78
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:08,000
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

79
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,500
Please sit down, Alexandra.

80
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:15,160
Dad, Richard--Alexandra's here.

81
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,200
Michigan needs a touchdown.

82
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:17,400
Three minutes to play.

83
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:19,100
Hi, Alexandra. Welcome.

84
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:20,300
Hello, Alexandra.

85
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,100
Yes, Michigan needs a touchdown.

86
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:25,300
One tiny little touchdown, with just three minutes to play.

87
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:27,300
You want Michigan to win.

88
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:28,100
How'd you guess?

89
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:43,000
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

90
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,900
What happened?

91
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:47,950
We forgot to turn the oven on.

92
00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:50,900
We did?

93
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:53,100
Philip, why don't you go

94
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:55,300
watch the last three minutes of the game.

95
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:58,300
I will serve coffee and pumpkin pie.

96
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:01,700
OK. I'll be back in a few minutes.

97
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:04,600
Robbie, would you bring the dessert plates.

98
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,200
And, Marilyn, would you pour coffee, please.

99
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:10,900
Sure, Ellen.

100
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:13,700
How was your Thanksgiving dinner, Alexandra?

101
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:15,500
Just wonderful, Mr. Stewart.

102
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,000
The Molinas are a large family.

103
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,200
I love being with them.

104
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:21,000
I'm glad you came by, Alexandra.

105
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,900
I am, too.

106
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:31,000
Touchdown! Touchdown! Touchdown!

107
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,600
Great Thanksgiving.

108
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:35,200
Lots to be thankful for.

109
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:37,500
Michigan scored a touchdown.

110
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:39,900
Alexandra came by.

111
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:43,600
And nobody misses Philip's famous apple pie.

112
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:46,488
Oh, Grandpa!
